  "worked_solution": "Let's use integration by parts. We set\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}u=x & \u21d2 & {u}^{\u2032}=1 \\\\ {v}^{\u2032}=\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x) & \u21d2 & v=\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSubstituting the above into the integration by parts formula, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int u{v}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x & =uv-\\int v{u}^{\u2032}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ \\int x\\cdot \\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & =x\\cdot \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)}{3}-\\int \\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)}{3}\\cdot 1\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we evaluate the integral and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\frac{x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)}{3}|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}-{\\int }_{0}^{\\pi /2}\\frac{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)}{3}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{3}x\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(3x)|}_{0}^{\\pi /2}+\\frac{1}{9}\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(3x){|}_{0}^{\\pi /2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}[\\frac{\\pi }{2}\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-0\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(0)] \\\\  & +\\frac{1}{9}[\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{3\\pi }{2})-\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0)] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{3}(-\\frac{\\pi }{2}-0)+\\frac{1}{9}(0-1) \\\\  & =-\\frac{\\pi }{6}-\\frac{1}{9}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
